1
00:00:00,900 --> 00:00:05,190
Every night, for six years, a mother lit a lamp in the same window.

2
00:00:07,290 --> 00:00:09,862
Her son had marched north with the legions.

3
00:00:10,462 --> 00:00:14,573
Rome sent no letters. No news. Nothing at all.

4
00:00:16,673 --> 00:00:19,821
The neighbours whispered that she was wasting good oil.

5
00:00:20,421 --> 00:00:25,804
But the baker downstairs always slipped her a little extra... and never said a word.

6
00:00:27,904 --> 00:00:29,960
Then one night, the oil ran out.

7
00:00:30,560 --> 00:00:33,862
And she wept... because she was sure it was a sign.

8
00:00:35,962 --> 00:00:39,450
But down in the dark street, a tired soldier stopped,

9
00:00:40,050 --> 00:00:43,112
and looked up at the only window with no light in it.

10
00:00:45,212 --> 00:00:47,230
He knew exactly which one it was.

11
00:00:47,830 --> 00:00:51,301
He had followed that light home, for three hundred miles.

12
00:00:53,401 --> 00:00:54,177
Mother.

13
00:00:55,277 --> 00:00:58,634
You can let it go out now. I'm home.

14
00:01:00,234 --> 00:01:02,294
Some lights never really go out.
